 * Whether an alert of a project is suppressed (#114), and why. AlertDispatcherService asks it
 * for every alert, so a mute or a maintenance window holds for every event and channel:
 * - `muted`: an active mute of the event (rule) or of the event and its subject (issue);
 * - `maintenance_window`: a one-off or weekly maintenance window of the project is in force;
 * - `maintenance_mode`: the latest report has the core `laravel-maintenance-mode` finding;
 * - `duplicate` (#143): an `infrastructure.failed` and a `health.failed` of the same check and
 *   fingerprint within DUPLICATE_MINUTES: the first one goes out, the other is kept as history;
 * - `throttled` (#22): the same event, project and subject already went to a channel within
 *   `excubia.alert_throttle_minutes` (an hour by default) at the same or a worse severity, so an
 *   escalation still goes out.
 * `project.token_changed` is a security event: only an explicit mute silences it, never a throttle. Schedule
 * events ignore maintenance mode: the schedule evaluation (#110) already pauses the tasks that
 * do not run then, so a task that runs in maintenance mode and misses still alerts.
 */";s:10:"attributes";a:0:{}s:9:"startLine";i:33;s:7:"endLine";i:197;s:11:"startColumn";i:1;s:9:"endColumn";i:1;s:15:"parentClassName";N;s:20:"implementsClassNames";a:0:{}s:15:"traitClassNames";a:0:{}s:18:"immediateConstants";a:6:{s:5:"MUTED";a:12:{s:18:"declaringClassName";s:36:"App\Services\AlertSuppressionService";s:21:"implementingClassName";s:36:"App\Services\AlertSuppressionService";s:4:"name";s:5:"MUTED";s:9:"modifiers";i:1;s:4:"type";N;s:5:"value";a:2:{s:4:"code";s:7:"'muted'";s:10:"attributes";a:6:{s:9:"startLine";i:35;s:7:"endLine";i:35;s:13:"startTokenPos";i:81;s:12:"startFilePos";i:1579;s:11:"endTokenPos";i:81;s:10:"endFilePos";i:1585;}}s:10:"docComment";N;s:10:"attributes";a:0:{}s:9:"startLine";i:35;s:7:"endLine";i:35;s:11:"startColumn";i:5;s:9:"endColumn";i:33;}s:18:"MAINTENANCE_WINDOW";a:12:{s:18:"declaringClassName";s:36:"App\Services\AlertSuppressionService";s:21:"implementingClassName";s:36:"App\Services\AlertSuppressionService";s:4:"name";s:18:"MAINTENANCE_WINDOW";s:9:"modifiers";i:1;s:4:"type";N;s:5:"value";a:2:{s:4:"code";s:20:"'maintenance_window'";s:10:"attributes";a:6:{s:9:"startLine";i:37;s:7:"endLine";i:37;s:13:"startTokenPos";i:92;s:12:"startFilePos";i:1627;s:11:"endTokenPos";i:92;s:10:"endFilePos";i:1646;}}s:10:"docComment";N;s:10:"attributes";a:0:{}s:9:"startLine";i:37;s:7:"endLine";i:37;s:11:"startColumn";i:5;s:9:"endColumn";i:59;}s:16:"MAINTENANCE_MODE";a:12:{s:18:"declaringClassName";s:36:"App\Services\AlertSuppressionService";s:21:"implementingClassName";s:36:"App\Services\AlertSuppressionService";s:4:"name";s:16:"MAINTENANCE_MODE";s:9:"modifiers";i:1;s:4:"type";N;s:5:"value";a:2:{s:4:"code";s:18:"'maintenance_mode'";s:10:"attributes";a:6:{s:9:"startLine";i:39;s:7:"endLine";i:39;s:13:"startTokenPos";i:103;s:12:"startFilePos";i:1686;s:11:"endTokenPos";i:103;s:10:"endFilePos";i:1703;}}s:10:"docComment";N;s:10:"attributes";a:0:{}s:9:"startLine";i:39;s:7:"endLine";i:39;s:11:"startColumn";i:5;s:9:"endColumn";i:55;}s:9:"DUPLICATE";a:12:{s